WEBVTT

00:00.604 --> 00:03.545
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.645 --> 00:06.946
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:06.981 --> 00:10.616
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.652 --> 00:13.619
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.655 --> 00:17.056
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.092 --> 00:20.460
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.495 --> 00:21.894
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:21.930 --> 00:23.362
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.398 --> 00:23.938
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:37.178 --> 00:40.313
Hey, welcome to Bonnie's
29th birthday party.

00:40.348 --> 00:43.549
I ca... I can't keep this up.

00:43.585 --> 00:45.151
She's 46.

00:45.186 --> 00:46.986
Here, we brought you guys
an orchid from Trader Joe's,

00:47.021 --> 00:48.321
because we don't know

00:48.356 --> 00:50.623
or care about
any of your interests.

00:53.461 --> 00:55.094
Well, I put together
some videos

00:55.130 --> 00:56.596
for Bonnie's party.

00:56.631 --> 00:58.397
Here we are on our honeymoon.

01:06.508 --> 01:08.407
Yeah, Cabo was great.

01:08.443 --> 01:10.676
We even went back
for our 10th anniversary.

01:23.124 --> 01:25.825
Better wrap it up,
honey, tide's coming in.

01:25.860 --> 01:27.493
Well, let's break for presents,

01:27.529 --> 01:29.695
but after that, I'll show you
Susie's birth video,

01:29.731 --> 01:31.130
and I'll tell you,
she fell out of there

01:31.166 --> 01:33.366
like an orange out
of an old dress sock.

01:33.401 --> 01:36.869
Ugh, I have to text Rupert
what a train wreck this is.

01:38.139 --> 01:40.540
Hey, I want real things.

01:46.915 --> 01:49.615
Kind of weird they're keeping
all our jackets in the tub.

01:54.756 --> 01:55.955
Bonnie?

01:55.990 --> 01:57.623
I told you, Joe,

01:57.659 --> 01:58.659
when we're alone,

01:58.693 --> 02:00.326
you can call me "Bonald."

02:00.361 --> 02:02.028
No, i-it's me, Brian.

02:02.063 --> 02:03.396
Is that your real name?

02:03.431 --> 02:05.831
I mean, are you...
are you okay?

02:05.867 --> 02:06.966
Sorry, am I
allowed on the bed?

02:07.001 --> 02:08.467
I guess so.

02:08.503 --> 02:09.535
What's wrong?

02:09.571 --> 02:10.670
Nothing.

02:10.705 --> 02:11.904
I have something
in my eye.

02:11.940 --> 02:13.172
Yes, you do.

02:13.208 --> 02:14.840
It looks
like sadness.

02:14.876 --> 02:16.309
Come on, you
can tell me.

02:16.344 --> 02:17.810
I'm your
neighbor's dog.

02:17.845 --> 02:18.978
I don't know.

02:19.013 --> 02:20.253
It's just that
when I was young,

02:20.281 --> 02:21.414
I had so many things

02:21.449 --> 02:23.382
I wanted to do
with my life,

02:23.418 --> 02:25.251
but now, I'm 46,

02:25.286 --> 02:28.688
and all I've ever done
is take care of Joe.

02:28.723 --> 02:30.223
And now you feel like
you never had a chance

02:30.258 --> 02:31.824
to be your true self.

02:31.859 --> 02:32.992
Yeah.

02:33.027 --> 02:34.360
I know just how you feel.

02:34.395 --> 02:35.928
I mean, I'm happy
that Peter found me

02:35.964 --> 02:37.496
and gave me a home, but

02:37.532 --> 02:38.664
sometimes I wonder

02:38.700 --> 02:40.266
if I'd be happier
on my own.

02:40.301 --> 02:41.601
Exactly.

02:41.636 --> 02:43.369
It's like sometimes,
I feel...

02:43.404 --> 02:44.570
Trapped?

02:44.606 --> 02:48.274
No, I was going to say,
"like the Von Trapps."

02:48.309 --> 02:50.843
You know, unable to leave
their home in Austria.

02:50.878 --> 02:53.913
Oh. Well, that still
is remarkably close.

02:53.948 --> 02:57.516
Thanks for being
so nice to me, Brian.

02:57.552 --> 03:00.019
Why are you scratching
behind my ear?

03:00.054 --> 03:01.420
I... I don't...
I don't know.

03:01.456 --> 03:02.955
I thought it might
make you feel better.

03:02.991 --> 03:05.391
It does feel kind of nice.

03:05.426 --> 03:06.726
You're a good girl.

03:06.761 --> 03:08.394
You're going to be okay.

03:16.004 --> 03:17.203
I'm... I'm sorry.

03:17.238 --> 03:18.404
I did... I didn't...
I didn't mean...

03:18.439 --> 03:19.872
No, it's okay.

03:19.907 --> 03:21.941
Um... I better go downstairs

03:21.976 --> 03:23.643
before Joe realizes
I'm gone.

03:23.678 --> 03:25.144
And before Peter

03:25.179 --> 03:27.280
gets into the stuff
that's not for the party.

03:27.315 --> 03:29.115
Aw, Halloween candy!

03:29.150 --> 03:31.317
Peter, get out
of the pantry.

03:31.352 --> 03:34.086
Ah, I can't believe I just
kissed my friend's wife.

03:34.122 --> 03:36.489
I'm a bigger scumbag than Spock.

03:36.524 --> 03:38.124
I heard that there
was a Romulan ship

03:38.159 --> 03:39.825
spotted in our sector,
which means...

03:39.861 --> 03:41.627
Hey, hey.

03:47.869 --> 03:49.835
Kids, this morning,
Principal Shepherd

03:49.871 --> 03:51.070
wanted to say a few words.

03:51.105 --> 03:52.405
Thank you, Mrs. Abbott.

03:52.440 --> 03:54.840
Uh, before I start,
are these the normal kids

03:54.876 --> 03:56.809
or kind of the
"dur, dur" ones?

03:56.844 --> 03:58.477
It's a healthy mix.

03:58.513 --> 03:59.513
Good morning, children.

03:59.547 --> 04:01.080
It's that time
of the year again

04:01.115 --> 04:03.449
to fulfill your
community service requirement

04:03.484 --> 04:04.850
by signing up
for volunteer work.

04:04.886 --> 04:06.319
Do we get to choose
our own jobs?

04:06.354 --> 04:07.586
No, no, no, no.

04:07.622 --> 04:09.422
The jobs will be
assigned randomly

04:09.457 --> 04:11.023
but the cooler
and prettier students

04:11.059 --> 04:12.191
have the better jobs.

04:12.226 --> 04:14.160
For instance, blonde
chick in the third row

04:14.195 --> 04:16.095
<i>will wash my car
this afternoon</i>

04:16.130 --> 04:18.297
while, Little Miss Frumpkin
with all the questions,

04:18.333 --> 04:20.199
will work in an
old folks' home.

04:20.234 --> 04:21.701
Is "frumpkin" good?

04:21.736 --> 04:23.903
No, no.

04:28.476 --> 04:29.942
Brian, what are you
doing up so late?

04:29.977 --> 04:31.677
Ah, I'm having
trouble sleeping.

04:31.713 --> 04:33.479
I got to tell you something.

04:33.514 --> 04:35.681
I kissed Bonnie last night.

04:35.717 --> 04:36.816
What?!

04:36.851 --> 04:38.117
I know! I know!
It was a huge mistake.

04:38.152 --> 04:39.952
So let's just do two
or three high-fives

04:39.987 --> 04:41.220
and then forget
it ever happened.

04:41.255 --> 04:43.055
Brian, if Joe finds out,
he'll kill you.

04:43.091 --> 04:44.123
Yeah, no kidding.

04:44.158 --> 04:45.157
That's why you can't
tell anybody.

04:45.193 --> 04:46.225
Promise me.

04:46.260 --> 04:47.360
Oh, don't worry.
Don't worry.

04:47.395 --> 04:48.828
I'm great at
keeping secrets.

04:48.863 --> 04:49.862
Well, except for
that one time

04:49.897 --> 04:51.697
you discovered
my hidden shame.

04:53.868 --> 04:55.201
Peter?

04:55.236 --> 04:56.302
Brian.

04:56.337 --> 04:58.137
I'm, uh, I'm sorry.

04:58.172 --> 05:00.339
I'm one of these guys now.

05:00.375 --> 05:03.609
I'm sorry, Brian, I'm sorry.

05:08.282 --> 05:09.382
Mrs. Parkhurst?

05:09.417 --> 05:11.183
I'm Meg, your new
student volunteer.

05:11.219 --> 05:15.354
Oh, you must be my
new student volunteer.

05:15.390 --> 05:16.922
Yeah, I just said that.

05:16.958 --> 05:18.591
What's your name, dear?

05:18.626 --> 05:20.025
It's Meg.

05:20.061 --> 05:21.761
Can... can I get
a new person?

05:21.796 --> 05:23.562
Nonsense, come in,

05:23.598 --> 05:24.997
and between you and me,

05:25.032 --> 05:27.600
I hate my new
student volunteer.

05:27.635 --> 05:29.168
That ugly little Meg.

05:29.203 --> 05:30.703
She says she's a girl,

05:30.738 --> 05:33.506
but she certainly has
a boy's body odor.

05:42.116 --> 05:43.416
Oh, come on in.

05:43.451 --> 05:45.751
Peter, Joe and Bonnie
are here for game night.

05:45.787 --> 05:46.952
Game night?

05:46.988 --> 05:48.821
Yeah, I figured it was
the least we could do,

05:48.856 --> 05:50.990
since you pulled up
a beheading video on your phone

05:51.025 --> 05:53.058
at their party
and showed it to everyone.

05:53.094 --> 05:55.161
It was really more about
how loud my phone can get.

05:55.196 --> 05:56.228
Peter, we're doing this.

05:56.264 --> 05:57.763
All right.

05:57.799 --> 05:59.265
But the Operation game
is out of batteries,

05:59.300 --> 06:00.800
so I'll have to
make the noise.

06:02.003 --> 06:03.135
You hear that?

06:03.171 --> 06:07.640
That's the sound
of bad surgery.

06:07.675 --> 06:09.208
All right,
I'm awesome at charades.

06:09.243 --> 06:10.409
Guys are going first.

06:10.445 --> 06:12.144
Okay, go.

06:12.180 --> 06:13.746
<i>Uh, About a Boy.</i>

06:13.781 --> 06:15.614
<i>Uh, Four...
Four Weddings and a Funeral.</i>

06:15.650 --> 06:17.249
<i>Uh, Nine Months.</i>

06:17.285 --> 06:18.451
<i>Notting Hill.</i>

06:18.486 --> 06:20.052
<i>Yes, it was Notting Hill.</i>

06:20.087 --> 06:22.188
I'm going to go
get more wine.

06:23.524 --> 06:25.090
Oh, hey.

06:25.126 --> 06:26.492
Hi, Brian.

06:26.527 --> 06:28.761
Um, listen,
about the other night.

06:28.796 --> 06:30.930
You haven't told anyone,
have you?

06:30.965 --> 06:32.431
No, no, of course not.

06:32.467 --> 06:34.133
I was going to
ask if you had.

06:34.168 --> 06:36.068
Hey, Brian,
can you bring me up a snack?

06:36.103 --> 06:37.436
I'm supposed to be in bed.

06:37.472 --> 06:39.405
Look, the other
night was great,

06:39.440 --> 06:40.573
but it was a mistake.

06:40.608 --> 06:41.740
You're right.

06:41.776 --> 06:44.477
Oh, man, what?

06:44.512 --> 06:45.911
Yeah, I me... I mean, there's...

06:45.947 --> 06:48.180
there's definitely some kind
of connection between us, but...

06:48.216 --> 06:49.782
I felt it, too,

06:49.817 --> 06:52.251
but maybe in another life, huh?

06:52.286 --> 06:54.186
Yeah, I guess
you're right.

06:54.222 --> 06:55.654
This could never work.

06:55.690 --> 06:57.823
Like porn movies
before sound.

07:04.332 --> 07:05.865
Ooh.

07:05.900 --> 07:07.766
Oh, there you are.

07:07.802 --> 07:09.134
Come on, Bonnie,
it's Joe's turn.

07:09.170 --> 07:11.504
Okay, here we go,
uh, uh, crippled guy...

07:11.539 --> 07:13.472
uh, cheating wife...

07:13.508 --> 07:16.275
uh, uh, cheating wife
of a crippled guy...

07:16.310 --> 07:19.345
Uh, dog... some... something
with a dog... uh, dog kiss.

07:19.380 --> 07:21.347
I-I-I, uh, I think
that's, uh, time.

07:21.382 --> 07:22.348
Your, your turn is over.

07:22.383 --> 07:23.616
Oh, sounds like, uh, sounds like

07:23.651 --> 07:25.584
dog kisses crippled guy's wife

07:25.620 --> 07:26.819
at your party.

07:26.854 --> 07:28.220
Wait, wait! I know it.

07:28.256 --> 07:30.022
The other night at your party,
Brian kissed Bonnie.

07:30.057 --> 07:31.123
What?

07:31.158 --> 07:33.292
Bonnie, is this true?

07:33.327 --> 07:34.994
Oh, my God.

07:35.029 --> 07:36.996
I know, making out with a dog?

07:37.031 --> 07:40.266
Can you even imagine a woman who
possibly does that for real?

07:50.874 --> 07:52.073
Uh, hi, Joe.

07:52.109 --> 07:53.374
Hi, Brian.

07:53.410 --> 07:55.977
Look, I-I want to apologize
for what happened.

07:56.012 --> 07:58.313
I-I-I didn't mean
to kiss Bonnie.

07:58.348 --> 08:00.148
Everybody had a little
too much to drink.

08:00.183 --> 08:01.716
It-it just happened.

08:01.751 --> 08:03.418
Uh, I hope we're still cool.

08:03.453 --> 08:04.853
Hey, don't worry about it.

08:04.888 --> 08:06.154
It was a crazy party.

08:06.189 --> 08:07.722
We ran out of salsa.

08:09.092 --> 08:10.925
How do you run out of salsa?

08:10.961 --> 08:12.660
Anyway, we're good.

08:12.696 --> 08:13.895
Really?

08:13.930 --> 08:15.096
Oh, thank God.

08:15.132 --> 08:17.398
I-I-I was worried you'd be mad.

08:17.434 --> 08:19.734
Mad? At my buddy, Brian?

08:19.769 --> 08:20.935
Not a chance.

08:20.971 --> 08:22.303
Hey, is that your car?

08:24.941 --> 08:26.107
What? No!

08:26.143 --> 08:27.108
Wh-what's he doing?

08:27.144 --> 08:28.710
My car was parked legally.

08:28.745 --> 08:31.246
Huh. Well, maybe your car

08:31.281 --> 08:33.882
violated some sort
of unspoken boundary.

08:33.917 --> 08:36.084
One that nobody
bothers to codify

08:36.119 --> 08:38.520
because it's just
common decency.

08:38.555 --> 08:40.221
Hey, Joe, is that the guy?

08:40.257 --> 08:41.257
Read your text, Jerry.

08:41.291 --> 08:42.957
Not supposed to say
you know me.

08:42.993 --> 08:44.859
Well, I hope your day
gets better, Brian,

08:44.895 --> 08:47.862
but, uh, I wouldn't
count on it.

08:54.838 --> 08:57.372
Boy, it wasn't easy
Mrs. Parkhurst,

08:57.407 --> 08:58.940
but I think we
got the nail

08:58.975 --> 09:00.642
that was poking
through your slipper.

09:00.677 --> 09:02.577
Well, you strike
me as someone

09:02.612 --> 09:04.279
who's never going
to get married,

09:04.314 --> 09:05.480
that's for sure.

09:05.515 --> 09:07.549
Now get me my itch cream.

09:07.584 --> 09:08.616
Is it in the drawer?

09:08.652 --> 09:09.817
Shut up!

09:09.853 --> 09:11.886
I'm trying to
hum atonally.

09:13.990 --> 09:15.190
Ugh.

09:25.001 --> 09:26.134
Here's your cream.

09:26.169 --> 09:27.302
See you Thursday.

09:28.705 --> 09:30.939
Oh, my God,
I can't believe I stole this.

09:30.974 --> 09:32.640
You know what?
I don't feel bad.

09:32.676 --> 09:34.175
That woman's a nightmare.

09:34.211 --> 09:37.045
Ooh, I should text this
to my best friend.

09:39.182 --> 09:40.782
Sick brooch!

09:40.817 --> 09:43.518
Adam, are you done with
that mayor homework, yet?

09:43.553 --> 09:46.221
It's called a bill, Mom.

09:50.627 --> 09:51.926
Hey, Brian,

09:51.962 --> 09:54.262
I, uh, feel that things
have been awkward between us,

09:54.297 --> 09:56.197
but just to show you
there's no hard feelings,

09:56.233 --> 09:57.265
can I buy you a drink?

09:57.300 --> 09:59.000
You know what?
Sure, thanks.

10:04.374 --> 10:06.808
What the hell happened?

10:09.045 --> 10:10.545
Ah! How do I walk?!

10:10.580 --> 10:12.780
Are these forever?!

10:12.816 --> 10:16.651
I also rubbed my butt on you
while you were unconscious.

10:16.686 --> 10:20.321
I like to put stuff online.

10:25.528 --> 10:26.894
Meg, Mom said that...

10:26.930 --> 10:28.696
Hey, what's all this stuff?

10:28.732 --> 10:30.798
Stuff I stole from
the old folks' home.

10:30.834 --> 10:32.166
But you should see
how they treat me.

10:32.202 --> 10:34.168
Meg, that's no excuse.

10:34.204 --> 10:35.370
Stealing is just plain...

10:35.405 --> 10:37.872
Oh, my God, is that
someone else's glasses?

10:37.907 --> 10:40.141
I love wearing other
people's glasses.

10:41.845 --> 10:43.878
Do I look like I stole
atomic secrets?

10:43.913 --> 10:44.979
You do.

10:45.015 --> 10:46.648
Wow, this is awesome.

10:46.683 --> 10:47.849
I want in.

10:47.884 --> 10:50.251
<i>And there's the
splitting headache</i>

10:50.287 --> 10:52.587
from wearing someone
else's glasses.

10:57.761 --> 11:00.995
Okay, Chris, here's a room
I haven't hit, yet.

11:01.031 --> 11:03.231
Here, follow my lead.

11:05.268 --> 11:06.334
Who's there?

11:06.369 --> 11:07.902
Why are you in my room?

11:07.937 --> 11:09.170
Oh, hi.

11:09.205 --> 11:12.240
You died, and I'm here
to take you to heaven.

11:12.275 --> 11:13.908
Um, upsy-daisy, here we go.

11:16.112 --> 11:17.745
Well, now that
I'm in heaven...

11:19.949 --> 11:21.049
Hurry, take everything,

11:21.084 --> 11:23.551
and be quick or we'll
be in bigger trouble

11:23.586 --> 11:25.853
than a fat guy
at a water park.

11:25.889 --> 11:28.189
Come on, Dad, let's go
on the water slide.

11:28.224 --> 11:29.957
I can't fit.

11:29.993 --> 11:32.060
I'm afraid
I'll get stuck.

11:32.095 --> 11:33.361
I'll just go in
the lazy river.

11:33.396 --> 11:34.462
But, Dad...

11:34.497 --> 11:37.465
No, son, this is
the life I've chosen.

11:38.501 --> 11:42.003
♪ When your day is long ♪

11:44.307 --> 11:46.574
♪ And the night ♪

11:46.609 --> 11:50.978
♪ The night is yours alone ♪

11:53.817 --> 11:55.750
♪ When you're sure you... ♪

12:06.796 --> 12:10.932
♪ Of this life... ♪

12:13.937 --> 12:15.336
Guys, thanks again
for doing this.

12:15.372 --> 12:17.405
Joe has been making
my life hell.

12:17.440 --> 12:18.406
Of course.

12:18.441 --> 12:19.640
All right,
now when Joe gets here

12:19.676 --> 12:20.808
we're just going to tell him

12:20.844 --> 12:21.976
he needs to lighten up on Brian,

12:22.011 --> 12:23.411
and then we'll all talk
this thing out

12:23.446 --> 12:25.012
so we can move past it.

12:25.048 --> 12:26.814
And then I get
to show my card trick?

12:26.850 --> 12:28.049
If there's time.

12:28.718 --> 12:29.884
Let's make this quick.

12:30.954 --> 12:32.954
What's going on?
What's all this?

12:32.989 --> 12:34.422
Joe, we all know what happened

12:34.457 --> 12:36.257
and we're here for you.

12:36.292 --> 12:38.926
But we think that you're taking
this revenge on Brian

12:38.962 --> 12:40.261
just a little too far.

12:40.296 --> 12:41.362
Yeah.
Yeah, I mean, come on.

12:41.398 --> 12:42.663
It's...it's like
enough is enough.

12:42.699 --> 12:44.766
The Triscuits are
the rosemary kind,

12:44.801 --> 12:46.634
not the regular kind.

12:46.669 --> 12:49.437
Me? I'm not the guy
who violated the sanctity

12:49.472 --> 12:51.139
of someone else's marriage.

12:51.174 --> 12:52.540
Well, you make a
good point, Joe,

12:52.575 --> 12:54.208
<i>and you're right,
this is Brian.</i>

12:54.244 --> 12:55.510
We all know
he don't care

12:55.545 --> 12:57.145
where he gets
his wick wet.

12:57.180 --> 12:58.946
Just ask
Quagmire's father.

12:58.982 --> 13:01.115
Okay, we might be getting
a little off track, here.

13:01.151 --> 13:02.283
Yeah, yeah, Brian's right.

13:02.318 --> 13:03.551
Joe, you're out of control.

13:03.586 --> 13:04.685
Even though Brian's
been trying

13:04.721 --> 13:05.953
to do my wife for years,

13:05.989 --> 13:07.855
and on some level,
I hate him for it.

13:07.891 --> 13:09.824
Oh, Brian's a complete dick,
we all know that,

13:09.859 --> 13:11.325
but I think we're
losing sight of the point

13:11.361 --> 13:13.461
that Bonnie's a weird slut
who's always letting you know

13:13.496 --> 13:14.662
she's open for business.

13:14.697 --> 13:16.631
What? When am I doing that?

13:16.666 --> 13:18.299
Oh, come on, when are
you not doing that?

13:18.334 --> 13:19.567
With that
boo-boo-baby voice,

13:19.602 --> 13:21.502
and that
still-breastfeeding rack.

13:21.538 --> 13:22.804
Give me some of that!

13:22.839 --> 13:24.138
I'm Bonnie's friend,

13:24.174 --> 13:25.574
but she could
sometimes get the mail

13:25.608 --> 13:27.408
in something other than a robe.

13:27.444 --> 13:28.743
Okay, so we're all
in agreement,

13:28.778 --> 13:30.478
Bonnie and Brian
are terrible people.

13:30.513 --> 13:32.079
Quagmire, I want you
to think of a card,

13:32.115 --> 13:33.881
but do not tell me what it is.

13:33.917 --> 13:35.016
Okay, enough.

13:35.051 --> 13:37.218
How dare any of you
criticize Bonnie?

13:37.253 --> 13:39.353
For years, she gave
up her own dreams

13:39.389 --> 13:40.688
to take care of Joe.

13:40.723 --> 13:42.156
And yeah, maybe
she kissed me.

13:42.192 --> 13:43.524
Maybe she needed to
because she feels

13:43.560 --> 13:44.759
so trapped in
her marriage.

13:44.794 --> 13:45.893
It's true.

13:45.929 --> 13:49.063
No one ever takes the time
to ask how I feel.

13:49.098 --> 13:50.898
Brian's the only one.

13:50.934 --> 13:52.066
They don't get us, Bonnie,

13:52.101 --> 13:53.501
and you deserve
better than this.

13:53.536 --> 13:55.036
We both do.

13:55.071 --> 13:56.103
You know what?

13:56.139 --> 13:57.972
Let's get out of here.

14:03.980 --> 14:06.948
Wow, we are zero for two
on interventions today.

14:09.152 --> 14:10.618
I'm not changing for nobody.

14:10.653 --> 14:13.287
You're no... you're the ones
with the problems.

14:19.427 --> 14:21.027
Ah, we did it.

14:21.062 --> 14:22.929
We don't need those
narrow-minded losers.

14:22.964 --> 14:24.697
This is so exciting.

14:24.733 --> 14:27.567
We can finally live the
lives we've always wanted.

14:27.602 --> 14:29.936
Like, I can finally start
my jewelry design business

14:29.971 --> 14:32.939
making earrings for tweens.

14:34.042 --> 14:35.908
Listen, hear that?

14:35.944 --> 14:37.944
That is the sound
of not making

14:37.979 --> 14:39.379
an enormous mistake.

14:39.414 --> 14:41.280
I think I hear it.

14:42.384 --> 14:45.084
Oh, hang on, looks
like we need gas.

14:45.120 --> 14:47.286
So do you have,
like, a credit card?

14:47.322 --> 14:49.555
Nope and no cash, either,

14:49.591 --> 14:51.391
but I don't care.

14:51.426 --> 14:53.626
I couldn't stand
another moment with Joe.

14:53.662 --> 14:57.196
It was torture just watching
him do a crossword puzzle.

14:57.232 --> 14:59.399
Hey, Bonnie, what's a
five-letter word for marriage?

14:59.434 --> 15:00.900
Fraud.

15:00.935 --> 15:02.568
Uh, it's got to start
with a "U".

15:02.604 --> 15:03.870
Union.

15:03.905 --> 15:05.738
Boy, you stink at this.

15:10.912 --> 15:13.713
Boy, it's just so
comforting to be here

15:13.748 --> 15:16.382
surrounded by
other people's memories.

15:18.653 --> 15:20.653
Back into the
sleeve with you.

15:20.689 --> 15:21.754
Can you hand me
another nylon

15:21.790 --> 15:24.223
that I use as a sock
with my huge beige shoe?

15:24.259 --> 15:26.426
Sure, and can you
hand me that ashtray?

15:26.461 --> 15:28.227
I might fire up
this pipe again.

15:28.263 --> 15:30.229
Chris, that's not
an ashtray.

15:30.265 --> 15:32.265
That's an urn
for someone's ashes.

15:32.300 --> 15:33.399
Really?

15:33.435 --> 15:34.801
Yeah, you've been
putting your pipe out

15:34.836 --> 15:36.002
in some guy.

15:36.037 --> 15:39.105
Oh, my God,
what are we doing?

15:39.140 --> 15:40.673
I feel awful.

15:40.709 --> 15:42.742
We need to give
everything back.

15:42.777 --> 15:44.677
Oh, you're right.

15:44.713 --> 15:46.612
We need to do
the right thing.

15:46.648 --> 15:48.748
<i>Like the dad
from Small Wonder.</i>

15:48.783 --> 15:49.849
All right, Vickie,

15:49.884 --> 15:51.451
time to shut you down
for the night.

15:51.486 --> 15:52.485
Good-night.

15:52.520 --> 15:55.888
See you tomorrow.

16:00.895 --> 16:03.029
Nah.

16:07.035 --> 16:09.502
She's really gone,

16:09.537 --> 16:11.471
and she took little
Susie with her.

16:11.506 --> 16:13.272
I miss that baby
more than anything.

16:16.411 --> 16:18.010
Oh, I guess she
left it here.

16:18.046 --> 16:19.212
Joe, I want you to know,

16:19.247 --> 16:21.347
I will not support
that relationship.

16:21.382 --> 16:22.949
If Brian and Bonnie
get married,

16:22.984 --> 16:24.117
I will not go.

16:24.152 --> 16:26.285
Although, Brian might want
me to be his best man.

16:26.321 --> 16:27.520
Then I'd have to go,

16:27.555 --> 16:29.388
and I'd have to dance.

16:29.424 --> 16:31.324
It would be weird to
be best man and not dance.

16:31.359 --> 16:32.658
And I'd have
to give a toast,

16:32.694 --> 16:34.193
and say that Bonnie's
the best thing

16:34.229 --> 16:35.228
that ever happened to him.

16:35.263 --> 16:36.395
You know, she is
the best thing

16:36.431 --> 16:38.231
that ever happened to him,
but don't worry, Joe.

16:38.266 --> 16:39.732
I'll only refer to you
as Bonnie's ex.

16:39.768 --> 16:41.868
You know, like,
"Bonnie has an ex,

16:41.903 --> 16:43.803
but Brian marks the spot."

16:43.838 --> 16:44.838
Oh, Peter, that's good.

16:44.873 --> 16:46.038
Thanks, babe.

16:46.074 --> 16:48.007
I hope Brian and Bonnie
are as happy as us.

16:48.042 --> 16:49.742
To Brian and Bonnie.

16:54.916 --> 16:56.849
Bad news:
the teenage runaways

16:56.885 --> 16:59.085
at table four were
not big tippers.

16:59.120 --> 17:01.687
We just need enough
money to get to Taos.

17:01.723 --> 17:02.989
That's like the capital

17:03.024 --> 17:05.024
of making and selling
your own jewelry.

17:05.059 --> 17:06.292
Okay, enough about
the jewelry.

17:06.327 --> 17:07.493
Do you even know
how to make it?

17:07.529 --> 17:09.162
I know how to
make jewelry.

17:09.197 --> 17:10.263
I just don't know

17:10.298 --> 17:13.366
how to make the
metal go into shapes.

17:13.401 --> 17:14.433
Hey, you know what'd be great?

17:14.469 --> 17:15.568
If you could talk with even

17:15.603 --> 17:17.403
a little bit of inflection
to your voice,

17:17.438 --> 17:20.072
so it doesn't sound so much
like a power sander.

17:20.108 --> 17:21.340
Screw you.

17:21.376 --> 17:23.276
You tweet things that
aren't worth tweeting.

17:23.311 --> 17:24.343
Well, I'm sorry,

17:24.379 --> 17:25.845
but Kim Kardashian
did get famous

17:25.880 --> 17:27.213
for making a sex tape.

17:27.248 --> 17:28.414
We all know that.

17:28.449 --> 17:29.515
That's not yours.

17:29.551 --> 17:30.850
And stop breathing
through your mouth.

17:30.885 --> 17:32.351
It's really annoying.

17:32.387 --> 17:33.352
I'm panting.

17:33.388 --> 17:34.720
That's how I sweat,
you dumb bitch.

17:34.756 --> 17:35.855
No, it isn't.

17:35.890 --> 17:37.423
Dogs sweat
through their paws.

17:37.458 --> 17:38.858
You're such a
know-it-all, Brian,

17:38.893 --> 17:41.227
you don't even know
about your own body.

17:41.262 --> 17:42.929
At least I've
had an orgasm.

17:43.832 --> 17:46.399
Wow, I am sorry.

17:46.434 --> 17:48.434
Look, th-this isn't us.

17:48.469 --> 17:49.469
This is just the no food

17:49.504 --> 17:50.803
and sleeping in
a car talking.

17:50.839 --> 17:52.305
We can make this work,

17:52.340 --> 17:54.273
like couples who
meet on Craigslist.

17:56.644 --> 17:58.477
You're not what you look like
in your picture.

17:58.513 --> 18:00.880
Let's get this over with.

18:00.915 --> 18:03.416
I wonder which one of us
is the murderer?

18:09.090 --> 18:11.090
Okay, we ditch this stuff
in the day room,

18:11.125 --> 18:12.792
and then I'm done
with my volunteer hours

18:12.827 --> 18:14.660
and we never come
back here again.

18:16.998 --> 18:18.164
Mrs. Parkhurst?

18:18.199 --> 18:22.101
Look at you two,
stealing from the elderly.

18:22.136 --> 18:24.170
You're worse than that
Juliette Lewis

18:24.205 --> 18:25.938
who makes out with dogs.

18:25.974 --> 18:27.306
Wait, is that a real thing?

18:27.342 --> 18:28.342
Where did you hear that?

18:28.376 --> 18:29.508
What are your sources?

18:29.544 --> 18:31.344
Listen, we're very sorry
we stole from you,

18:31.379 --> 18:32.511
but you have it all back now,

18:32.547 --> 18:34.280
so we cool, right?

18:34.315 --> 18:37.516
You know I should call
the police on you.

18:37.552 --> 18:38.584
The police?!

18:38.620 --> 18:41.854
Or maybe, instead,
we do things my way.

18:41.890 --> 18:43.422
What's that?

18:43.458 --> 18:45.491
You will spend time with us

18:45.526 --> 18:47.526
every afternoon after school,

18:47.562 --> 18:49.929
doing jigsaw puzzles,

18:49.964 --> 18:51.998
reading us the newspaper,

18:52.033 --> 18:56.469
listening to poorly remembered
stories that have no point.

18:56.504 --> 18:58.304
You monster.

18:58.339 --> 18:59.505
Sit down.

19:00.842 --> 19:02.708
Now I feel some
dementia coming.

19:02.744 --> 19:04.377
Feed me pudding
while I grip

19:04.412 --> 19:06.812
your wrist in terror.

19:06.848 --> 19:09.215
Ah, this isn't
my house.

19:12.921 --> 19:14.487
See, if I make
under 20 grand

19:14.522 --> 19:15.554
for 20 years,

19:15.590 --> 19:17.056
my film school debt
just goes away.

19:17.091 --> 19:18.357
That's a government rule.

19:18.393 --> 19:20.026
Bonnie?

19:20.061 --> 19:21.127
Joe?

19:21.162 --> 19:22.828
How did you find me?

19:22.864 --> 19:25.197
Love is a powerful compass.

19:25.233 --> 19:28.200
Any time I quiet my mind
and clear my heart,

19:28.236 --> 19:30.069
it always leads me to you.

19:30.104 --> 19:32.038
Plus, dirtbag here has
a chip in his ear.

19:32.073 --> 19:33.472
I do?
Damn it.

19:33.508 --> 19:35.508
No wonder Peter's so good
at hide-and-seek.

19:35.543 --> 19:37.476
You're under the canoe
in Quagmire's yard.

19:37.512 --> 19:38.978
Son of a bitch!

19:39.013 --> 19:41.414
Bonnie, I understand
now why you left.

19:41.449 --> 19:44.383
Over the years, I probably have
become too dependent on you,

19:44.419 --> 19:47.653
and I'm sorry if you've
had to put your dreams

19:47.689 --> 19:49.555
on hold because of me.

19:49.590 --> 19:51.190
Oh, Joe.

19:51.225 --> 19:52.992
But I'm here to
fight for you, Bonnie.

19:53.027 --> 19:54.994
And if you're willing
to come back home,

19:55.029 --> 19:58.197
I promise I'll spend the rest
of my days taking care of you,

19:58.232 --> 20:01.033
just the way you've
always taken care of me.

20:01.069 --> 20:03.235
Of course,
I want to come home, Joe.

20:03.271 --> 20:04.770
I love you.

20:09.043 --> 20:12.111
Wow, I guess just
call me Cupid, huh?

20:12.146 --> 20:14.113
You're welcome.

20:14.148 --> 20:15.414
Ow! Damn it!

20:17.552 --> 20:19.285
Hey, Bri, came to try
that apple pie

20:19.320 --> 20:20.386
you were texting about.

20:20.421 --> 20:21.754
Oh, you're shot.

20:25.727 --> 20:27.526
Well, Chris and I sure
learned a lot this week.

20:27.562 --> 20:29.295
<i>Ha, you think you
learned a lot.</i>

20:29.330 --> 20:30.629
I had quite
an adventure.

20:30.665 --> 20:31.630
You know what guys?

20:31.666 --> 20:33.265
We only got like
15 seconds left.

20:33.301 --> 20:34.567
We're going to have
to do these at the same time.

20:34.602 --> 20:35.735
Let's race.

20:35.770 --> 20:37.136
And... go.

20:37.171 --> 20:38.337
So Chris and I learned
that just 'cause people are old,

20:38.373 --> 20:40.006
that doesn't mean
you should steal from them.

20:40.041 --> 20:41.474
Bonnie didn't let you
stir the paint, did she?

20:41.509 --> 20:43.476
No. But I am done messing
around with neighbors' wives.

20:43.511 --> 20:45.077
Here's an invitation
to Donna's birthday party.

20:45.113 --> 20:46.645
'Cause maybe then I'd like it.
Hey, let me see that.

20:46.681 --> 20:48.381
You rascal.
Same old Meg.

20:48.416 --> 20:50.282
And the winner is:
Nobody.

20:50.318 --> 20:52.685
Especially not you.
Good night.

20:52.686 --> 20:54.686
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru